  "reference_protocol": "Complete statements go to both public file modes and the pinned reference shell on separate lines. Compare output, return codes, normalized diagnostics and persisted catalog/rows/rowids/integrity. Expected namespace results are never rewritten or filtered.",
  "implementation": "The parser normalizes only a lexical main qualifier to its object name; quoted periods remain single identifiers. The independent Core replay consumes qualifier/name tokens and checks exact declared spelling. Unknown schemas are rejected by that narrower Core boundary using the original schema token rendering. The broad parser still retains other schema names for the legacy conformance fixture. Legacy main lookup and column bindings now resolve normalized main objects while preserving source qualifiers; public execution remains in Core.",
  "full_evaluation_correction": "The first final SQL comparisons passed, but the existing attached-schema join exposed that validating unknown schemas in the context-free broad parser was too early. Namespace admission moved to the Core token replay. The legacy conformance evaluator resolves normalized main names and binds original source qualifiers. The failed unit log/plan/receipts are retained; final checks use a new runtime source checkpoint and fresh seeds.",
  "proof_scope": "Existing certified character/token replay connects the accepted source to the AST. A runtime regression checks two coexisting table names and rejects forged swaps between qualified and quoted-period targets. Existing Core/source/storage proof domains remain; no full SQL namespace-equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh-seed survey share named families and a generator; their 18 remaining failures are not a global compatibility percentage.",
